(292922, 20139, 7438, '<td valign="top">I cut the camera out of an old magazine ad and crumpled it a bit, then shot it against a white backdrop. I bumped up the brightness and contrast in Photoshop to get the white I wanted, and to burn out the top/left edges.<br/>But I think this would''ve worked much better with a crumpled image of a yellow flower against a blue sky for example. Something a bit more lively than the camera ad.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments people :)</td>', 'I cut the camera out of an old magazine ad and crumpled it a bit, then shot it against a white backdrop. I bumped up the brightness and contrast in Photoshop to get the white I wanted, and to burn out the top/left edges.But I think this would''ve worked much better with a crumpled image of a yellow flower against a blue sky for example. Something a bit more lively than the camera ad. Thanks for the comments people :)', '2003-05-09 08:46:37.000000', NULL, 0),
